(557364, 55522, 7467, '<td valign="top">Thank you all very much for the kind comments! I am really excited about this first win. This site has been a great benefit to me in helping improve my photo skills.<br/> <br/>A little more detail on the pic: I took this thru my dining room window of the Cardinal perched on top of the rod that supports the bird feeder mounted on the rail of my sundeck. She looked so pathetic bracing against the high wind, cold and blowing snow. <br/> <br/>I used my Nikon 80-400 mm AF VR lens. I was "zoomed" to about 230mm. This shot was taken without a tripod, just me leaning against the window frame and hoping the VR feature on the lens (vibration reduction) worked - as the light level was a bit low and the camera was at 1/40 sec. (And yes we keep the feeder full!).<br/> <br/>Thanks again,<br/>Drake</td>', 'Thank you all very much for the kind comments! I am really excited about this first win. This site has been a great benefit to me in helping improve my photo skills. A little more detail on the pic: I took this thru my dining room window of the Cardinal perched on top of the rod that supports the bird feeder mounted on the rail of my sundeck. She looked so pathetic bracing against the high wind, cold and blowing snow.  I used my Nikon 80-400 mm AF VR lens. I was "zoomed" to about 230mm. This shot was taken without a tripod, just me leaning against the window frame and hoping the VR feature on the lens (vibration reduction) worked - as the light level was a bit low and the camera was at 1/40 sec. (And yes we keep the feeder full!). Thanks again,Drake', '2004-01-26 06:51:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(557372, 55522, 3306, '<td valign="top">Great capture. You definitely deserve the ribbon on this one!</td>', 'Great capture. You definitely deserve the ribbon on this one!', '2004-01-26 06:58:22.000000', NULL, 0),
