(561526, 55587, 16713, '<td valign="top">Excellent Shot!!! I think that with a little bit more of DOF the shot could take a level higher!<br/> <br/>   Ricardo</td>', 'Excellent Shot!!! I think that with a little bit more of DOF the shot could take a level higher!    Ricardo', '2004-01-28 23:32:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(561596, 55574, 14350, '<td valign="top">I agree with Siggi  This is awesome and should never have 1''s 2''s or even 4''s <br/>I notice that people do that on a lot of shots<br/>Maybe the person voting thinks 1''s are the highest???????????</td>', 'I agree with Siggi  This is awesome and should never have 1''s 2''s or even 4''s I notice that people do that on a lot of shotsMaybe the person voting thinks 1''s are the highest???????????', '2004-01-29 00:39:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(561700, 55581, 6999, '<td valign="top"><b>Your Critique Club moment</b> <br/> <br/>got to agree with the noise comments - an image tidying programme would help no end: but I should also say that that''s as much to do with the challenge as anything. I think of NG photography as being technically highly assured - clean, exact, quite high contrast - and this is almost the opposite.<br/> <br/>Which is not to say I don''t quite like it, just that it was never going to do so well in this challenge. I like the gentle toning of the pic, the movement of colour in the skies - I think I''d almost like it more <i>without</i> the lump of land in it, so that it would be more abstract.<br/> <br/>That land is perhaps part of the problem - or rather your placement of it within frame. It isn''t forming a major part of the composition, not being far enough into frame for that, but also it''s not working to frame anything, balance anything, and of itself it''s pretty dull to me - a lump of rock and snow.<br/> <br/>Your title confuses too - I''d expect to see a storm cloud, or some more present threat with blue skies, whereas your entire image is blue, with just a hint of gentle pink. <br/> <br/>Ed</td>', 'Your Critique Club moment  got to agree with the noise comments - an image tidying programme would help no end: but I should also say that that''s as much to do with the challenge as anything. I think of NG photography as being technically highly assured - clean, exact, quite high contrast - and this is almost the opposite. Which is not to say I don''t quite like it, just that it was never going to do so well in this challenge. I like the gentle toning of the pic, the movement of colour in the skies - I think I''d almost like it more without the lump of land in it, so that it would be more abstract. That land is perhaps part of the problem - or rather your placement of it within frame. It isn''t forming a major part of the composition, not being far enough into frame for that, but also it''s not working to frame anything, balance anything, and of itself it''s pretty dull to me - a lump of rock and snow. Your title confuses too - I''d expect to see a storm cloud, or some more present threat with blue skies, whereas your entire image is blue, with just a hint of gentle pink.  Ed', '2004-01-29 05:32:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(561715, 55640, 7687, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>KING,<br/>I have to agree, this image is extraordinarily sharp, I can see why though...I also have a 50 f/1.8.  The first thing that grabbed me about this image was the colors of the rock in the upper left and the colors of the fish.  The dark background works perfectly and the positioning of the fish (composition) is extremely well done.  There really isn''t much to critique about this image so I''ll stop right here and say, great work!<br/> <br/>Quadrajet</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! KING,I have to agree, this image is extraordinarily sharp, I can see why though...I also have a 50 f/1.8.  The first thing that grabbed me about this image was the colors of the rock in the upper left and the colors of the fish.  The dark background works perfectly and the positioning of the fish (composition) is extremely well done.  There really isn''t much to critique about this image so I''ll stop right here and say, great work! Quadrajet', '2004-01-29 06:33:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(561748, 55587, 9906, '<td valign="top">From the Critique Club<br/> <br/>I really don''t know what I comments I can add that haven''t already been pointed out by previous commentors or your outstanding score and ribbon!<br/> <br/>This is simply an awesome shot.  The focus, DOF and composition are right on.  In fact the only things that I don''t like about the shot (and very minor at that) are totally beyond your control.  I don''t really like the background (looks fake because, well, it''s fake!  It''s a zoo...) and the small amount of glare that you did get off the glass.<br/> <br/>Nice work and congrats on the ribbon!<br/>TC</td>', 'From the Critique Club I really don''t know what I comments I can add that haven''t already been pointed out by previous commentors or your outstanding score and ribbon! This is simply an awesome shot.  The focus, DOF and composition are right on.  In fact the only things that I don''t like about the shot (and very minor at that) are totally beyond your control.  I don''t really like the background (looks fake because, well, it''s fake!  It''s a zoo...) and the small amount of glare that you did get off the glass. Nice work and congrats on the ribbon!TC', '2004-01-29 07:47:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(562077, 55522, 16739, '<td valign="top">VERY NICE , I LOVE THE MOVEMENT OF THE SNOW</td>', 'VERY NICE , I LOVE THE MOVEMENT OF THE SNOW', '2004-01-29 15:48:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(562831, 55772, 6999, '<td valign="top"><b>Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>Hi Alice<br/> <br/>Good score - pity that the standard was so high for that challenge, else you''d have placed so much better.<br/> <br/>For me there was something not quite satisfying about this shot - I mean that it didn''t quite get me as I though it might have been able to. I know it''s a tricky shot to get, but I don''t think that should sway opinions of it. I think I felt that the framing of the shot was not good: I''d rather have seen a touch more location, perhaps. Also I wonder about your placement of the seals'' heads in frame, and relative to the bodies: maybe showing more of the mother would enable you to contrast the relative sizes of the two and to put the real subject (that moment of contact) into a stronger place compositionally. I can imagine then the lines of the bodies forming a happier graphic element to the image. Just thoughts and imaginings, or course.<br/> <br/>More purely technically, of course, there is nothing to criticise. And of course, its absolutely fitting for the challenge: I just feel that you slightly missed the ''art'' element that NG seems to like in its nature shots.<br/> <br/>Ed</td>', 'Critique Club  Hi Alice Good score - pity that the standard was so high for that challenge, else you''d have placed so much better. For me there was something not quite satisfying about this shot - I mean that it didn''t quite get me as I though it might have been able to. I know it''s a tricky shot to get, but I don''t think that should sway opinions of it. I think I felt that the framing of the shot was not good: I''d rather have seen a touch more location, perhaps. Also I wonder about your placement of the seals'' heads in frame, and relative to the bodies: maybe showing more of the mother would enable you to contrast the relative sizes of the two and to put the real subject (that moment of contact) into a stronger place compositionally. I can imagine then the lines of the bodies forming a happier graphic element to the image. Just thoughts and imaginings, or course. More purely technically, of course, there is nothing to criticise. And of course, its absolutely fitting for the challenge: I just feel that you slightly missed the ''art'' element that NG seems to like in its nature shots. Ed', '2004-01-30 05:41:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(562972, 55707, 14614, '<td valign="top">Thanks to all who took the time to comment.  I learned loads from your remarks (scale, setting and background dirt - that lead oxide kept flaking off!)  I''m working on composition and lighting and appreciate the positive reinforcement.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-01-30 09:20:55.</i></td>', 'Thanks to all who took the time to comment.  I learned loads from your remarks (scale, setting and background dirt - that lead oxide kept flaking off!)  I''m working on composition and lighting and appreciate the positive reinforcement.', '2004-01-30 09:20:28.000000', '2004-01-30 09:20:55.000000', 0),
(563113, 55152, 9906, '<td valign="top">From the Critique Club<br/> <br/>Shannon, this is an awesome picture!  I love the 3 dimensional feeling here.  There is a definate sense of depth.  The neutral color scheme works very well also.  The earthy tones of the soil and grasses go well with the tones of the animal itself.<br/> <br/>Under <i>ideal</i> circumstances, there are a couple of things that might have made this shot even more potent.  This includes framing the shot so the animal is looking <i>into</i> the frame instead of out of it.  I would LOVE to see more detail in the animals fur especially in the face areas.  None of these things really detracts from the shot, but would maybe add to it...<br/> <br/>Great work,<br/>TC</td>', 'From the Critique Club Shannon, this is an awesome picture!  I love the 3 dimensional feeling here.  There is a definate sense of depth.  The neutral color scheme works very well also.  The earthy tones of the soil and grasses go well with the tones of the animal itself. Under ideal circumstances, there are a couple of things that might have made this shot even more potent.  This includes framing the shot so the animal is looking into the frame instead of out of it.  I would LOVE to see more detail in the animals fur especially in the face areas.  None of these things really detracts from the shot, but would maybe add to it... Great work,TC', '2004-01-30 12:54:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(563218, 55522, 16188, '<td valign="top">A Critique Club comment:<br/> <br/>The mood is beautifully captured and I like the framing.  One of the things that is serendipitous but why it works so well is the color balance (reds, orange, rust, cream against the bluish gray of the perch and the warm brownish grays in the background).  The sharpness of the bird''s feet gripping the perch is nice.  I keep wanting to see more detail in the face but I don''t know if any more was available since the rest of the bird is so clear.</td>', 'A Critique Club comment: The mood is beautifully captured and I like the framing.  One of the things that is serendipitous but why it works so well is the color balance (reds, orange, rust, cream against the bluish gray of the perch and the warm brownish grays in the background).  The sharpness of the bird''s feet gripping the perch is nice.  I keep wanting to see more detail in the face but I don''t know if any more was available since the rest of the bird is so clear.', '2004-01-30 15:37:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(563235, 55807, 16188, '<td valign="top">A Critique Club comment: <br/> <br/>The adjustments you made do give the shot a night time feel.  The eye keeps trying to straighten the trees against the horizon but I think the larger trees in the background on the left correct for that for the most part.  The light source seems too bright for the moon but one''s mind automatically makes allowances for that because of the overall night time effect.  Still, it''s a little bit distracting in the sky (the way the light falls on the snow both background and foreground is lovely).</td>', 'A Critique Club comment:  The adjustments you made do give the shot a night time feel.  The eye keeps trying to straighten the trees against the horizon but I think the larger trees in the background on the left correct for that for the most part.  The light source seems too bright for the moon but one''s mind automatically makes allowances for that because of the overall night time effect.  Still, it''s a little bit distracting in the sky (the way the light falls on the snow both background and foreground is lovely).', '2004-01-30 15:48:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(563358, 55718, 5158, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/><b>Initial thoughts/My opinion</b> <br/>Nice looking antique ceramics, a bit soft/unsharp and the selection of background and light is not too well.<br/> <br/><b>Content/Composition</b> <br/>The two bottles are really nice and fit well to the challenge topic. Also how you placed them and cropped the image is OK. <br/>The main issue of improvement is regarding the background and the light. I would have chosen a darker one to better contrast the not too dark ceramics. Maybe also with some shadows on the ground and the background. <br/>Speaking of shadow I want to address the light: it is set rather flat. The light is set very homogeneous and the objects are well exposed everywhere. However, this style would be more appropriate for an archaeological journal or catalogue: it''s rather clinical without too much atmosphere. For instance some soft light from the right would have produced some shadows and thus more depth.<br/> <br/><b>Camera work -technically</b> <br/>Focus is OK, but the DOF seems a bit narrow: the ceramic in the back is less sharp. White balance and exposure are fine.<br/> <br/><b>Digital Processing - Technical</b> <br/>A bit more sharpening would be fine, also  border.<br/> <br/><b>Fits the challenge</b> <br/>Yes, it fits well, could envision it in an archaeological article.<br/> <br/>Good luck for your upcoming submissions<br/> <br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club  Initial thoughts/My opinion Nice looking antique ceramics, a bit soft/unsharp and the selection of background and light is not too well. Content/Composition The two bottles are really nice and fit well to the challenge topic. Also how you placed them and cropped the image is OK. The main issue of improvement is regarding the background and the light. I would have chosen a darker one to better contrast the not too dark ceramics. Maybe also with some shadows on the ground and the background. Speaking of shadow I want to address the light: it is set rather flat. The light is set very homogeneous and the objects are well exposed everywhere. However, this style would be more appropriate for an archaeological journal or catalogue: it''s rather clinical without too much atmosphere. For instance some soft light from the right would have produced some shadows and thus more depth. Camera work -technically Focus is OK, but the DOF seems a bit narrow: the ceramic in the back is less sharp. White balance and exposure are fine. Digital Processing - Technical A bit more sharpening would be fine, also  border. Fits the challenge Yes, it fits well, could envision it in an archaeological article. Good luck for your upcoming submissions ', '2004-01-30 17:18:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(563396, 55811, 5158, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/><b>Initial thoughts/My opinion</b> <br/>Great clear image, speaking of lines, texture and a wonderful sky. To me it does not work for National Geographic too well.<br/> <br/><b>Content/Composition</b> <br/>You captured at the right moment a wonderful place: as your title says the image speaks by its clear and crisp appearance. The leading line of the bridge, the texture of its wood and of the surrounding field work very well together. That the walk leads to the small forest makes the horizon more interesting and the great clouds make the image complete.<br/>I really can''t see any flaw here.<br/> <br/><b>Camera work -technically</b> <br/>You did a great job technically: focus, exposure and white balance all set very well.<br/> <br/><b>Digital Processing - Technical</b> <br/>Also regarding the post processing no issue to be mentioned. Especially the sharpening is well done: not too much, just right.<br/> <br/><b>Fits the challenge</b> <br/>To my personal taste the image comes short here: I cannot envision a story that comes with the image. The title would have been a possibility to give the viewer an idea in what context to place the beautiful image.<br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club  Initial thoughts/My opinion Great clear image, speaking of lines, texture and a wonderful sky. To me it does not work for National Geographic too well. Content/Composition You captured at the right moment a wonderful place: as your title says the image speaks by its clear and crisp appearance. The leading line of the bridge, the texture of its wood and of the surrounding field work very well together. That the walk leads to the small forest makes the horizon more interesting and the great clouds make the image complete.I really can''t see any flaw here. Camera work -technically You did a great job technically: focus, exposure and white balance all set very well. Digital Processing - Technical Also regarding the post processing no issue to be mentioned. Especially the sharpening is well done: not too much, just right. Fits the challenge To my personal taste the image comes short here: I cannot envision a story that comes with the image. The title would have been a possibility to give the viewer an idea in what context to place the beautiful image.', '2004-01-30 17:46:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(563503, 55587, 6900, '<td valign="top">WOW and Welcome back.  And yes, we remember second often here. :)<br/> <br/>M</td>', 'WOW and Welcome back.  And yes, we remember second often here. :) M', '2004-01-30 20:18:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(563559, 55744, 16672, '<td valign="top">I can''t say anything</td>', 'I can''t say anything', '2004-01-30 21:35:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(563573, 55483, 16672, '<td valign="top">Your picture the color is nice the saturation is good. The problem is your eyes are drawn to the awful eyesore the bad burning you did on the top of the weight machine it kills everything else in your image because I can''t avoid looking at it and I find it the death of your work. I am sorry nobody else is addressing it but its true. You may want to try in the future to try mask that part then lower the bright level there plus think abut the angle and what you see as the light source or object reflecting light. Thank you for he picture though!</td>', 'Your picture the color is nice the saturation is good. The problem is your eyes are drawn to the awful eyesore the bad burning you did on the top of the weight machine it kills everything else in your image because I can''t avoid looking at it and I find it the death of your work. I am sorry nobody else is addressing it but its true. You may want to try in the future to try mask that part then lower the bright level there plus think abut the angle and what you see as the light source or object reflecting light. Thank you for he picture though!', '2004-01-30 22:00:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(563587, 55706, 16672, '<td valign="top">Needs contrast but the picture composition is nice. The character and etc is good.</td>', 'Needs contrast but the picture composition is nice. The character and etc is good.', '2004-01-30 22:33:47.000000', NULL, 0),
